+## Subtopics
+
+### Optimized Resampling Point Calculation
+This variant focuses on the specific computation at each resampling point, applying early termination and normal encoding without other acceleration techniques [S1, unofficial]. It structures the calculation into three parts: transfer function calculation, lighting model calculation, and interpolation calculation [S1, unofficial]. It reduces lighting calls from eight to one per point while maintaining seven interpolation operations for color, opacity, and normal vector [S1, unofficial].
 
 ## Operating characteristics
 **Time and Memory Complexity:**
-*   The optimization reduces the computational load by significantly lowering the number of lighting calculations [S1].
-*   The calculation amount is small compared to the previous method [S1].
+*   The optimization reduces the computational load by significantly lowering the number of lighting calculations [S1, unofficial].
+*   The calculation amount is small compared to the previous method [S1, unofficial].
 
 **Measured Performance:**
-*   The optimization led to about a 300% improvement in performance for the new renderer [S2, unofficial].
-*   The new mapper performs about 35% faster than its OpenGL version 1 counterpart [S2, unofficial].
-*   The new mapper performs about 135% faster than the `vtkFixedPointVolumeRayCastMapper`, with shading enabled [S2, unofficial].
-*   Complex images (e.g., projectile penetration into reinforced concrete) can be rendered in two minutes, and simpler scenes (e.g., air explosion shock waves) in less than one minute [S1].
